BRXCOMPD                                                         MAINTC command

Use the BRXCOMPD command to compile C programs that are part of the bREXX
runtime library. The files are compiled with imbedded debug and trace code.

The format of the BRXCOMPD command is:
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| BRXCOMPD | c_fn [parm_fn|DBGBRX [GCC options]]                              |
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Usage Notes:

1. Set up the proper minidisk search order with the BRXSRCHD command before
   using this command.

2. The BRXCOMPD produces an output TEXT file from the compilation on the
   A-disk.
